<title>POLAND: KPW CLEARS POLISH MINES WKSM FOR PUBLIC TRADE.</title>
<headline>KPW CLEARS POLISH MINES WKSM FOR PUBLIC TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities</p>
<p>Commission (KPW) has cleared for public trade existing shares</p>
<p>and a new issue of raw materials mine Wroclawskie Kopalnie</p>
<p>Surowcow Mineralnych SA, the KPW said in a statement.</p>
<p>The KPW cleared 403,000 existing shares, of which 132,950</p>
<p>will be sold in a public offering by the state treasury and</p>
<p>80,600 new shares to be offered to the firm's employees.</p>
<p>			     No Of Shares	   Subscription</p>
<p>			     Offered		  Period</p>
<p> state treasury shares 132,950		  June 2-6</p>
<p> employee tranche	 80,600		  June 2-6</p>
<p> Lead Manager:	   BRE brokerage</p>
<p> Price* (PLN):	   26/shr</p>
<p> Lead Underwriter:     n/a</p>
<p>Note: * - price for the shares sold by the state treasury. The</p>
<p>company seeks a parallel market listing.</p>
<p>EARNINGS DATA	    1997 forecast	1996</p>
<p>(in mln of PLN)</p>
<p> Net profit:	     1.8		     1.0</p>
<p> Sales:		    n/a		    37.5</p>
<p>Main Shareholders:</p>
<p> state treasury   - 53 pct of shares</p>
<p>Bank Zachodni SA - 35.5 pct of shares</p>
<p>No of existing shares: 403,000</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
